Restore the icon theme the user actually had, instead of a hardcoded
"Adwaita", when ChromaLeon stops overriding org.gnome.desktop.interface's
icon-theme key.

Both places that stop using the synthetic "ChromaLeon" theme -- extension.js's
disable(), and themeUtils.js's updateIconPack() when recolor-folders is off --
reset icon-theme to the LITERAL STRING "Adwaita", regardless of what the user
had before ChromaLeon ever touched the key. That is upstream's bug for anyone
not already on Adwaita; this repo just happens to reproduce it concretely,
because nix/home/profiles/portable.nix declares Papirus-Dark.

This is NOT the "make ChromaLeon recolor Papirus" change. That was investigated
and rejected: ChromaLeon's icon engine is a find-and-replace over ~24 literal
Adwaita hex fills, and Papirus-Dark shares none of them, ships no scalable/
directory at all (fixed pixel-size dirs, every stanza Type=Fixed), and recolors
folders by symlinking a pre-drawn variant rather than substituting a fill.
Teaching it Papirus would be a second recoloring backend, not a bugfix, and
this repo already implements that mechanism properly in
nix/home/desktop/quickshell/qml/wallpaper/Icons.qml. See
nix/packages/chromaleon.nix's header.

FAILURE MODE IF DROPPED: nix/home/base/gnome-extensions.nix pins the icon
toggles false, so this never fires from the declared config alone. But GNOME's
Extensions app lets anyone flip recolor-folders on by hand, writing straight to
ChromaLeon's gschema and bypassing home-manager, which only re-asserts declared
keys on the next switch. The first time that happens, unpatched code swaps
icon-theme from Papirus-Dark to the literal "Adwaita" the moment the toggle
goes back off -- not back to Papirus-Dark, because upstream never recorded it.
Nothing self-heals that key.

Shipped as a real .patch rather than a postPatch substituteInPlace because it
adds an instance field and threads a new parameter through a call site, neither
of which a substitution can express -- and because a patch that stops applying
fails the build at the rev bump that invalidated it, where a vanished
substitution pattern would silently no-op.

